ainst new variants as  they arise  either you know by having sam you know  actual  you know available residual clinical  samples  that correspond to given variance or by  uh  perhaps your quality controlling their  assays on  your defined templates or rnas that  you have the same sequence as these  variants just to ensure that the assays  are  you know still performing uh uh you know  as expected  uh in terms of you know diagnosing uh  as far as kobe 2 in someone who may have  a different variant  thank you so much and again i want to  thank our audience for these great  questions coming in  our next question aside from the public  health value  is there a clinical role for  distinguishing  sgtf from non-sgtf  variants sure um  i think the main clinical role uh would  be  uh in terms of of therapeutics  i mean even the vaccines i i would  consider that kind of half clinical have  public health because  um you know often you would be dealing  with someone who's vaccinated and it's  of interest to know  if they have a variant you know and  that's why the vaccine may not have  worked  but in terms of direct clinical utility  i think it's therapeutics and  and the area where it's become most  important  as i indicated in the talk is with you  know antibody therapy where  that can uh make a difference and so  uh i think that's gonna be a key area  we don't really have a lot of  information on uh  variants and other therapeutics um but  that certainly is something that could  play out in the future  uh you know whether certain variants you  know  as we've seen with other viruses are  less uh sensitive to  rendezvous or other antivirals that come  down the pike  that will become important as well and  then uh as a clinician i can tell you  that  even if it's not clinically important  your clinicians will be asking you  um uh asking the clinical lab you know  is this  you know variant x um is that why this  patient  you know is not doing well even if even  if it's not  real